From daa3a6ab883d7ff1f5addd69a935f7b915688727 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Uwe Augustin <Info@FlapsOnline.de>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 14:18:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 08/22] OV: move the sensor and touch calibration out of
 OpenVarioMenu

XCSoar itself is going to offer both calibrations on an OpenVario, so
that a pilot does not have to quit to the start menu for them.  The
code moves unchanged into its own file, which both programs can link,
instead of being copied.  The touch calibration takes the display and
the event queue as parameters, because XCSoar has to hand over the
screen and the input devices to the script just as the menu does.
---
 build/ov.mk              |   1 +
 src/OV/Calibrate.cpp     | 102 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/OV/Calibrate.hpp     |  26 ++++++++++
 src/OV/OpenVarioMenu.cpp |  83 +------------------------------
 4 files changed, 131 insertions(+), 81 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 src/OV/Calibrate.cpp
 create mode 100644 src/OV/Calibrate.hpp

